INT. PLANETARY SURVEY SHIP, BRIDGE - NIGHT

A curving window of stars. Four stations, four lit consoles. A klaxon starts mid-conversation.

CAPTAIN ELEANOR VOSKUIJLEN (50s, silver braid) stands at the center. COMMANDER RAJIV ABERNATHY (40s) hunches at navigation. LIEUTENANT SASHA TEMPLETON-OYELOWO (30s) works the comm. ENSIGN BRODERICK "BROD" PAPADAKIS (20s, wide-eyed) mans the shield board.

VOSKUIJLEN
Report!

ABERNATHY
Asteroid field dead ahead, ma'am. Debris cloud--

TEMPLETON-OYELOWO
Captain, I'm picking up a distress signal inside it--

BROD
Shields at forty percent!

VOSKUIJLEN
Divert power from the forward arrays.

ABERNATHY
Diverting. Captain, the cloud is expanding faster than--

TEMPLETON-OYELOWO
Signal's repeating. Says "last survivor, Aurora Station."

BROD
Thirty percent! Twenty!

VOSKUIJLEN
Hold your nerve, Ensign. Rajiv, can we thread it?

ABERNATHY
Barely. Three seconds, and we'll clip the rim.

VOSKUIJLEN
Then clip it. Sasha, hail the survivor. Tell them we're coming.

TEMPLETON-OYELOWO
Aye, Captain.

The ship shudders. Alarms scream. Then, one by one, they fall silent. The window shows a calm field of drifting rock. Brod sags over his board.

BROD
Shields... holding.

VOSKUIJLEN
Good. Now find our survivor.
